+## UBU-D0338: Guided acquisition and channel alternatives serve ordinary life logistics
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §1 and §21.1.3. Resolves `UBU-Q0182`'s product contract; extends `UBU-D0319` without claiming implementation acceptance.
+
+Keep UbU's primary identity as a privacy-first life-logistics system. Offer guided camera acquisition and voice/text/form choices to all users without a disability label. Describe specific tested access benefits and limitations rather than inferring accessibility from camera availability.
+
+Adopt optional, target-specific guidance with one usable instruction at a time, explicit uncertainty, exact correction, finite retry/time limits and a reachable exit or manual route. Support nonvisual acquisition and the declared assistive-technology routes through the same candidate review and admission surface. Channel and assistance choices grant no capture, disclosure, retention, planner-Preference or external-action authority; current privacy and restricted-attention rules govern every route.
+
+Require DESIGN.md §21.1.3's consented user trials and condition-specific outcomes before enabling or claiming the affected workflows. Publish tested combinations, correction/assistance burdens, failures, fallbacks and gaps; a manual fallback cannot prove guided-camera access. This resolves product positioning and the guidance/access acceptance contract, not measured accessibility or universal coverage. `UBU-Q0177`, `UBU-Q0168` and `UBU-Q0183` retain hardware, numerical-profile and release-allocation scope.
