 ### Question
 
 How should camera-positioning guidance and voice/text/form alternatives improve accessibility without positioning UbU primarily as an accessibility product?
 
 ### Current direction
 
 Delta §17.20. Test framing/label acquisition, unavailable vision or speech, restricted attention, assistive technologies and privacy constraints with users. Describe access benefits as part of ordinary life logistics; do not infer universal accessibility from having a camera.
 
 ### Resolution
 
-Open.
+Resolved by `UBU-D0338`: DESIGN.md §1 and §21.1.3 keep access benefits within UbU's ordinary life-logistics purpose and specify optional bounded camera guidance, nonvisual feedback, exact correction, useful voice/text/form and assistive-technology routes, private output and restricted-attention limits. Consented user trials must establish workflow-specific usefulness, control, review and privacy before delivery claims; failures and fallback gaps remain visible. This resolves the product contract, not implementation or measured accessibility. Hardware, numerical profiles and delivery allocation remain under `UBU-Q0177`, `UBU-Q0168` and `UBU-Q0183`; no universal-access claim is established.
 
